rem as it starts, its lines as if typed at its prompt, after its namespace (newns), its window's
rem console at /dev and its note group (the login's own, as /rom/lib/profile does them for rc).
rem Through the /lib union, a /lib/basic/profile.bas on the RAM disk or a card takes the place of
rem this one (the ROM's): BASIC's lines or rc's (cd /sd/0, a variable, a program loaded ...).
